  "notes": "<h6>Alignment and tie-ins</h6><ol><li>Start at S0-S017-Bore station 7,700 ft on the east approach to Cleveland Avenue. Set the transfer into Morse Road inside surveyed public ROW. The tie moved about 81 ft back along the RFP bore to clear the retail corner.</li><li>Continue west on Morse through the ramp junction and beneath both I-71 structures. At the marked Morse–Sinclair intersection, cross the Morse carriageways on the Sinclair leg and continue north on Sinclair. Keep pits and turning room in permitted public workspace.</li><li>Cross SR 161 on the Sinclair–Huntley street connection. Shift the desktop trace about 12 ft west across the junction so it clears the parcel mapped at the northeast corner. Follow Huntley north and make the public-road tie at Schrock near S0-S019-Bore station 7,770 ft.</li></ol><h6>Parcel and road evidence</h6><p>Intersected the entire option with 887 unique Franklin County Auditor polygons retrieved along Morse, Sinclair and Huntley. The previous trace overlapped about 2,419 ft of polygons with taxable commercial or residential use codes. The revised line has zero measured overlap with that group. Municipal land, coded ROW and unclassified county polygons at road crossings need legal ROW confirmation. The route follows the county LBRS road geometry except for the public-road tie-ins and the shift at SR 161. The aerial exhibit shows the two intersection approaches.</p><p><a href=\"https://mapping.dublin.oh.us/arcgis/rest/services/Accela/MapServer/2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Franklin County cooperative street centerlines</a> · <a href=\"https://gis.franklincountyohio.gov/hosting/rest/services/ParcelFeatures/Parcel_Features/FeatureServer/0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Franklin County Auditor parcels</a> · <a href=\"https://maps.ohio.gov/image/rest/services/osip_most_current/ImageServer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ohio statewide aerials</a></p><h6>Crossings and permits</h6><ul><li><strong>Morse under I-71.</strong> Columbus and ODOT District 6 should review the street occupancy and state access-control limits together. Obtain the bridge and ramp plans for SFNs 2508192 and 2508222. Show foundation clearances, storm and signal utilities, traffic control and public pit limits. Include the Sinclair ramp-terminal interfaces in the same District 6 kickoff. <a href=\"https://tims.dot.state.oh.us/ags/rest/services/Assets/Bridge_Inventory/MapServer/0/query?where=SFN+IN+%28%272508192%27%2C%272508222%27%29&amp;outFields=SFN%2CSTR_LOC_CARRIED%2CINVENT_FEAT%2CMAIN_STR_TYPE_CD%2CCULVERT_LEN&amp;outSR=4326&amp;returnGeometry=true&amp;f=pjson\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ODOT bridge records</a> · <a href=\"https://www.transportation.ohio.gov/business/permits/row-permits\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ODOT utility and ROW permits</a></li><li><strong>Sinclair at Bull Moose Run.</strong> ODOT inventories SFN 2561507 as an 84-ft culvert at alternative station about 15,359 ft. The Columbus sidewalk contract independently identifies the culvert. Retrieve the road drainage and sidewalk record sheets, locate barrel and apron limits and fit an independent trenchless profile. If clearance is tight, test the other public road side with the City. <a href=\"https://tims.dot.state.oh.us/ags/rest/services/Assets/Bridge_Inventory/MapServer/0/query?where=SFN+IN+%28%272561507%27%29&amp;outFields=SFN%2CSTR_LOC_CARRIED%2CINVENT_FEAT%2CMAIN_STR_TYPE_CD%2CCULVERT_LEN&amp;outSR=4326&amp;returnGeometry=true&amp;f=pjson\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Culvert inventory</a> · <a href=\"https://columbus.legistar.com/LegislationDetail.aspx?FullText=1&amp;GUID=54408C0C-0160-4456-ADB3-521583655A29&amp;ID=6502994\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Columbus sidewalk contract</a></li><li><strong>Unnamed Morse drainage.</strong> ODOT flowline 21951 meets the option at about 853 ft. Aerial and inventory review found no confirmed road barrel at that location. Carry a storm-record and field check before assigning a separate crossing quantity. <a href=\"https://tims.dot.state.oh.us/ags/rest/services/MapViewers/Hydraulic_Engineering_Stream_Order/MapServer/0/query?objectIds=21951&amp;outFields=OBJECTID%2CCOMID%2CFTYPE%2CFCODE&amp;outSR=4326&amp;returnGeometry=true&amp;f=pjson\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ODOT flowline 21951</a></li><li><strong>SR 161 and Huntley.</strong> Verify the state-route crossing and the municipal handoff at SR 161 with Columbus, ODOT District 6 and Worthington. Use Worthington’s telecom ROW intake, utility exposure and applicable sewer inspection requirements for its stretch of Huntley. <a href=\"https://www.worthington.org/298/Right-of-Way-Work-Permits\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Worthington ROW permits</a></li><li><strong>Rail.</strong> The route turns north east of the rail bridges over Morse. County rail linework shows no intersection on this option. Keep the surveyed work footprint east of railroad property.</li></ul>"
}
